        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Ancient Near East</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Cyrus the Great</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 600 BCE – 530 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 600 BCE, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambyses-i">Cambyses I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">King of Anshan</a>, and Mandane, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astyages">Astyages</a>, King of Media</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">Around December 530 BCE; the accounts conflict: killed in battle with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massagetae">Massagetae</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>), with the Derbices (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ctesias">Ctesias</a>) or with the Dahae (Berossus), or dead peacefully at his capital (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xenophon">Xenophon</a>)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">King of Anshan</a> from 559 BCE under Median overlordship; King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and of Media after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecbatana">Ecbatana</a> in 550 BCE; King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkad">Akkad</a> and King of the Four Corners of the World from 539 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>; the conquests of Media, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Neo-Babylonian Empire</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-cylinder">Cyrus Cylinder</a>; the return of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-captivity">Babylonian captivity</a>; tolerance of local customs and religions; government through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satraps</a>; his tomb at Pasargadae</span></div>
